From 9f3b871997c249c3079e10e57fb6eb7f2563c3b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cerXXXX <polyakovia2009@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:20:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: print "First frame presented" once the compositor shows
 the wallpaper

A launcher that freezes the engine (SIGSTOP while on power saver) has to
know when a frame with the wallpaper's content is on the screen, or it
freezes an empty surface. Wayland frame callbacks of frames that showed
content mark their screen as presented; once every wallpaper's screen is,
"First frame presented" is printed. Videos count from mpv's first
decoded frame (MPV_EVENT_PLAYBACK_RESTART), not the empty texture before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
